            <section class=3D"post-full-content">
                <div class=3D"post-content">
                    <p><br><a href=3D"https://www.zuar.com/products/runner/=
mongo-db?ref=3Dzuar.com" target=3D"moredetail">MongoDB</a> is a <strong>fle=
xible, document-orientated, <a href=3D"https://www.zuar.com/blog/whats-the-=
difference-between-sql-nosql/" target=3D"moredetail">NoSQL</a> database pro=
gram</strong> that can scale to any enterprise volume without compromising =
search performance. MongoDB also integrates easily with <strong>ETL/data st=
aging platforms like <a href=3D"https://www.zuar.com/products/runner/?ref=
=3Dzuar.com" target=3D"moredetail">Zuar Runner</a></strong>.</p><p>Need a <=
strong>quick reference cheat sheet</strong> for common MongoDB commands? Wh=
ether you=E2=80=99re just learning or need a refresher, we=E2=80=99ve got y=
ou covered.</p><p><strong>Related Article:</strong></p><figure class=3D"kg-=
card kg-bookmark-card"><a class=3D"kg-bookmark-container" href=3D"https://w=
ww.zuar.com/blog/connecting-tableau-to-mongodb/" target=3D"moredetail"><div=
 class=3D"kg-bookmark-content"><div class=3D"kg-bookmark-title">Connecting =
Tableau &amp; MongoDB: The Key to Data-Driven Success</div><div class=3D"kg=
-bookmark-description">Learn how to integrate MongoDB with Tableau to trans=
form complex datasets into insightful, interactive visualizations.</div><di=
v class=3D"kg-bookmark-metadata"><img class=3D"kg-bookmark-icon" src=3D"htt=
ps://www.zuar.com/blog/content/images/2022/07/Unicorn-Favicon-64x64.ico" al=
t=3D""><span class=3D"kg-bookmark-author">News &amp; Education</span><span =
class=3D"kg-bookmark-publisher">Team Zuar</span></div></div><div class=3D"k=
g-bookmark-thumbnail"><img src=3D"https://www.zuar.com/blog/content/images/=
2023/11/tableau-mongodb-image.png" alt=3D""></div></a></figure><h2 id=3D"in=
itiation-creation-commands"><strong>Initiation &amp; Creation Commands</str=
ong></h2><p>Below are commands that relate to initiating and creating a dat=
abase. These are commands that are essential when you=E2=80=99re beginning.=
</p><h3 id=3D"starting-and-stopping-the-mongodb-database-"><strong>Starting=
 and Stopping the MongoDB Database:</strong></h3><p>sudo service mongod sta=
rt<br>sudo service mongod stop</p><h3 id=3D"accessing-the-mongodb-with-shel=
l-"><strong>Accessing the MongoDB With <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/=
wiki/Shell_script?ref=3Dzuar.com" target=3D"moredetail">Shell</a>:</strong>=
</h3><p>mongo --host localhost:27017</p><h3 id=3D"showing-all-databases-"><=
strong>Showing All Databases:</strong></h3><p>Show dbs</p><h3 id=3D"showing=
-the-current-database-">Showing the Current Database:</h3><p>db</p><h3 id=
=3D"switching-to-a-different-database-or-creating-a-database-"><strong>Swit=
ching to a Different Database or Creating a Database:</strong></h3><p>use n=
ameofdb<br><br></p><p><em><strong>Need to improve your data strategy? </str=
ong></em><a href=3D"https://www.zuar.com/services/data-strategy?ref=3Dzuar.=
com" target=3D"moredetail"><em><strong>Learn how</strong></em></a><em><stro=
ng> Zuar can customize data strategy and solutions to meet your organizatio=
n=E2=80=99s growing data needs. </strong></em></p><figure class=3D"kg-card =
kg-image-card"><img src=3D"https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/0ctYA5pAxrg9p2=
AAZGP31oobZIklNwz1_iMfWs0seiiVqRaJ5SDzqTrHl9TNrZW9kc00Ze5iCqp2o0FW6_45VYQzJ=
s80Mx5lisQUSqOgOQeDoaANH33qXyq1J2_ZD2LmHILm_ic=3Ds0" class=3D"kg-image" alt=
=3D"Coding collections and records in a MongoDB database" loading=3D"lazy">=
</figure><h2 id=3D"collection-record-commands">Collection &amp; Record Comm=
ands</h2><p>These are the basic <a href=3D"https://docs.mongodb.com/manual/=
core/databases-and-collections/?ref=3Dzuar.com" target=3D"moredetail">comma=
nds for collections</a> and records in a MongoDB. Whether you=E2=80=99re ne=
w to MongoDB or it=E2=80=99s been awhile, these are your bread and butter c=
ommands.</p><h3 id=3D"creating-a-collection-"><strong>Creating a Collection=
:</strong></h3><p>db.createCollection("collectionname")</p><h3 id=3D"droppi=
ng-a-collection-"><strong>Dropping a Collection:</strong></h3><p>db.collect=
ionname.drop() </p><h3 id=3D"showing-all-collections-in-a-database-"><stron=
g>Showing All Collections in a Database:</strong></h3><p>NOTE: You=E2=80=99=
ll need to execute the =E2=80=9Cuse dbname=E2=80=9D command before you can =
run this command.</p><p>show collections<br>show tables</p><p>Or you can us=
e this code:<br>db.getCollectionNames()</p><h3 id=3D"inserting-a-record-int=
o-a-collection-"><strong>Inserting a Record into a Collection:</strong></h3=
><p>db.collectionname.insert({"field1: "content", "field2": "morecontent", =
"field3": "moredata"})</p><h3 id=3D"updating-a-record-in-a-collection-"><st=
rong>Updating a Record in a Collection:</strong></h3><p>NOTE: This will onl=
y update the first match, and not for duplicates. Anything not specified wi=
ll be deleted from the record.</p><p>db.collectionname.update({"field1": "c=
ontent"}, {field1: "updateddata=E2=80=9D})</p><h3 id=3D"deleting-a-record-"=
>Deleting a Record:</h3><p>db.collectionname.remove({"field1": "content=E2=
=80=9D})</p><h3 id=3D"deleting-all-the-records-in-a-collection-"><strong>De=
leting ALL the Records in a Collection:</strong></h3><p>db.collectionname.r=
emove({ })</p><h3 id=3D"counting-the-records-in-a-collection-"><strong>Coun=
ting the Records in a Collection:</strong></h3><p>db.collectionname.find().=
count() </p><h3 id=3D"counting-the-records-by-a-specific-field-value"><stro=
ng>Counting the Records by a Specific Field Value</strong></h3><p>db.collec=
tionname.find({ field1: 'content' }).count()</p><h3 id=3D"listing-a-collect=
ion-s-records-"><strong>Listing a Collection=E2=80=99s Records:</strong></h=
3><p>db.collectionname.find()</p><p>db.collectionname.find().pretty()</p><h=
3 id=3D"listing-records-with-matching-values-of-specific-fields-"><strong>L=
isting Records with Matching Values of Specific Fields:</strong></h3><p>db.=
 collectionname.find({"field1": "matchers"})</p><h3 id=3D"multiple-matching=
-values-"><strong>Multiple Matching Values:</strong></h3><p>db. collectionn=
ame.find({"field1": "matchers", "field2": "secondmatchingvalue"}) </p><h3 i=
d=3D"finding-a-single-record-"><strong>Finding a Single Record:</strong></h=
3><p>db. collectionname.findOne({"field1": "content"})<br></p><p><em><stron=
g>Does your organization need data staging expertise? <a href=3D"https://ww=
w.zuar.com/services/data-staging?ref=3Dzuar.com" target=3D"moredetail">Zuar=
's technical consultants can make your life easier.</a></strong></em><br></=
p><figure class=3D"kg-card kg-image-card"><img src=3D"https://lh6.googleuse=
rcontent.com/ZKeQPdOaWZUTauOFnErLdJ4AtDGJFYW3soZH9Rwo5ESGbOBh8HY9kyIBxs8OH2=
TxorjIQFXXqgsCVMJmDPkh3nqO_FVBNKlsMW8dXlyQhvvGIUCT1nsXY-7OK49VRwk_1HKlo90=
=3Ds0" class=3D"kg-image" alt=3D"" loading=3D"lazy"></figure><h2 id=3D"aggr=
egation-operations-for-mongodb"><strong>Aggregation Operations for MongoDB<=
/strong></h2><p>Common operations you=E2=80=99ll need for filtering and agg=
regating records within a collection.</p><h3 id=3D"aggregating-an-expressio=
n-"><strong>Aggregating an Expression:</strong></h3><p>db.collectionname.ag=
gregate([{$group : {_id : "$operator", num_of_records : {$sum : 1}}}])</p><=
h3 id=3D"key-aggregation-filtering-operations-"><strong>Key Aggregation Fil=
tering Operations:</strong></h3><ul><li><strong>$project</strong>: Changes =
keys and values of &nbsp;a set of records.</li><li><strong>$match</strong>:=
 Reduces the number of records for the next stage.</li><li><strong>$group</=
strong>: Groups records by one or two keys.</li><li><strong>$sort</strong>:=
 Sorts the records for the next stage.</li><li><strong>$skip</strong>: Skip=
s forward a specified number of records.</li><li><strong>$limit</strong>: L=
imits the number of records to search through.</li><li><strong>$unwind</str=
ong>: Unwinds records that are using arrays.</li><li><strong>$all</strong>:=
 finds all records that belong to the array.</li></ul><h3 id=3D"using-great=
er-than-or-less-than-"><strong>Using Greater Than or Less Than:</strong></h=
3><ul><li><strong>$gt</strong>: Greater Than</li><li><strong>$gte</strong>:=
 Greater Than or Equal</li><li><strong>$lt</strong>: Lesser Than</li><li><s=
trong>$lte</strong>: Lesser Than or Equal</li><li><strong>$eq</strong>: Equ=
al</li></ul><p><strong>Examples:</strong></p><p>db.collectionname.find({ vi=
ews: { $gt: 2 } })<br>db.collectionname.find({ views: { $gte: 2 } })<br>db.=
collectionname.find({ views: { $lt: 2 } })<br>db.collectionname.find({ view=
s: { $lte: 2 } })<br></p><p><em><strong>Want to simplify and automate your =
data management? <a href=3D"https://www.zuar.com/contact?ref=3Dzuar.com" ta=
rget=3D"moredetail">Contact Zuar</a> to learn how they can help you refine =
your data strategy.</strong></em></p><figure class=3D"kg-card kg-bookmark-c=
ard"><a class=3D"kg-bookmark-container" href=3D"https://www.zuar.com/blog/d=
ata-warehouse-strategy-questions/" target=3D"moredetail"><div class=3D"kg-b=
ookmark-content"><div class=3D"kg-bookmark-title">Data Warehouse Strategy: =
What Questions Should You Ask l Zuar</div><div class=3D"kg-bookmark-descrip=
tion">In today=E2=80=99s modern world, data is anywhere and everywhere. At =
Zuar[https://www.zuar.com/], our mission is to help you build a modern stra=
tegy,leverage the correct tools, automate your process, protect your inform=
ation, and improve your business through the use of data. One way to accomp=
lish these=E2=80=A6</div><div class=3D"kg-bookmark-metadata"><img class=3D"=
kg-bookmark-icon" src=3D"https://www.zuar.com/blog/favicon.ico" alt=3D""><s=
pan class=3D"kg-bookmark-author">Zuar | Blog</span><span class=3D"kg-bookma=
rk-publisher">Team Zuar</span></div></div><div class=3D"kg-bookmark-thumbna=
il"><img src=3D"https://www.zuar.com/blog/content/images/2020/09/data-wareh=
ouse.jpg" alt=3D""></div></a></figure><h2 id=3D"miscellaneous-commands"><br=
><strong>Miscellaneous Commands</strong></h2><p>Here are a few helpful misc=
ellaneous commands that you=E2=80=99ll need to define your MongoDB.</p><h3 =
id=3D"creating-an-index-"><strong>Creating an <a href=3D"https://www.zuar.c=
om/blog/sql-indexes-guide/" target=3D"moredetail">Index</a>:</strong></h3><=
p>db.collectionname.createIndex({ title: 'text' })</p><h3 id=3D"listing-all=
-indexes-"><strong>Listing All Indexes:</strong></h3><p>db.collectionname.g=
etIndexes()<br>db.collectionname.getIndexKeys()</p><h3 id=3D"hiding-and-unh=
iding-indexes-">Hiding and Unhiding Indexes:</h3><p>db.collectionname.hideI=
